# Durchkriechstein (Schliefstein) beside the Falkensteinkirche, back-layer
# prop (D-057): a rounded limestone boulder 4 tiles wide and 3 tall. Rows
# 0-31 = the boulder over the level's invisible solid tiles (drawn = solid,
# D-038): its top is row 0 (the corners round off by <= 2 px over the first
# 5 px), shaded as a round mass lit from the top left (w / i / m), a w lip
# along the top, m cracks, two m cup marks (the saint's and the devil's
# traces), g/G moss tufts. Rows 32-47 = the low tunnel (the empty tile row):
# the boulder rests on two short feet with polished w/i mouth edges, d
# interior with a k ceiling shadow, a lighter m/i patch where the far opening
# lets the light in, worn m floor stones. Resi is drawn over it while
# crawling. No outline (back layer). Drawn by the pixel-artist with a
# throwaway script; the grid is the source.
sprite = durchkriechstein
size   = 64x48
origin = 32,48
anim   = idle frames=1
